Changes since v2:
 - 1/6, 2/6: code unchanged. Messages corrected: the overshoot folds
   every remaining entry (not just the next) and length_last_sg drops to
   0 rather than being inflated; the [2, 1] example's result is
   config-dependent; the mapped-pass heap overflow is now mentioned; the
   kernel-doc quote about partial coverage, which is not in the tree, is
   replaced by what the kernel-doc does say; the ->length clobber only
   shows with in_mapped_nents == 0; s390 selects NEED_SG_DMA_LENGTH only
   with PCI.
 - 3/6 replaces v2's "guard sg_split_phys()/sg_split_mapped() against
   zero-nents splits": v2 skipped those splits and returned
   ZERO_SIZE_PTR as out[k] (not a list; a caller walking it oopses), and
   it did not reject past-the-end requests in the same shape. v3 fixes
   it in sg_calculate_split(): -EINVAL for a past-the-end request, one
   zero-length end-marked entry for a valid zero-size split at the end.
   The copiers' nents guards are gone (no split has 0 entries any more).
 - new 4/6: no zero-length first entry when skip (or a split start)
   lands on an entry boundary or an empty entry.
 - new 5/6: -EINVAL for nb_splits <= 0 and skip < 0.
 - 6/6 (was 3/5 + 5/5): the suite now lands after all the fixes; T8b
   expects a one-entry zero-length list; new cases T8c (skip == total,
   zero-size splits), T8d/T8e (past-the-end requests), T17 (split
   starting at an empty entry), T18 (invalid arguments); every case also
   checks out_mapped_nents >= 1, the shape of zero-size splits and that
   no non-empty split starts with a zero-length entry; T6 moved to the
   edge-aligned group (it is not a mid-entry case); the divergent cases
   now check each split's CPU entry count (with sg_nents(), before
   walking it) and end marker; outputs are
   freed through deferred KUnit actions so a failed assertion doesn't
   leak them; stale comments fixed (T8b reference before T8b existed,
   a nonexistent backing_out parameter).

